    description: "## Origin\n\nCascade from WI-jusih-navod-mogib-disot-busub-rapof-susol-baniv data pass (2026-05-15).\n\n## Verdict\n\nReport `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wi-jusih-data-pass-20260515/report.md` measured rescue counts and false-positive risk across three targets (pretix v4.1.0 reused run, wagtail/bakerydemo, lutris/website) and a 15-repo non-Django Python corpus.\n\nAll five candidate names landed in bucket A (ship in α-conservative allow-list):\n\n| Candidate                | Net rescues (3 repos) | FP risk (15-repo non-Django corpus) |\n|--------------------------|----------------------:|------------------------------------:|\n| HierarkeyForm            |                    17 |                                0/15 |\n| FilterSet                |                    34 |                                0/15 |\n| Serializer (DRF family)  |                    82 |                                0/15 |\n| Page (Wagtail)           |                    13 |                                0/15 |\n| ModelAdmin (Django admin)|                    29 |                                0/15 |\n\nApplicationRecord (Rails) was excluded up front — Rails 5+ host apps generate it in-tree, so the existing short-name fallback in inheritance.py:175-194 already rescues it.\n\n## Implementation envelope (from report §\"α-conservative allow-list — recommended implementation envelope\")\n\n1. Gate the allow-list by framework activation (`LinkerActivation(frameworks=[...])`) — Wagtail entries activate only when Wagtail is detected, DRF entries only when DRF is detected, etc. This eliminates cross-framework FP by construction.\n2. Match on simple name OR FQN-prefixed qualified name (`HierarkeyForm` or `hierarkey.forms.HierarkeyForm`, etc.). Reuse `_short_base_name`-style normalization.\n3. Inherit INV-zuhub discipline: when the allow-list matches an UNQUALIFIED short name AND `build_short_name_collisions` reports an in-tree collision, mark the match as a fallback (`confidence <= 0.5`, `meta[\"disambiguation_fallback\"] = True`). Empirical collision rate on the three targets was 0/175, but consistency with the existing framework-base linker discipline is cheap.\n4. Initial entries (alphabetical within each framework activation):\n   - django_orm activation: `HierarkeyForm` / `hierarkey.forms.HierarkeyForm` → honorary `forms.Form`; `ModelAdmin` / `django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` → honorary admin dispatch.\n   - django-filter activation: `FilterSet` / `django_filters.FilterSet` / `WagtailFilterSet` → honorary FilterSet dispatch surface.\n   - drf activation: `Serializer` / `ModelSerializer` / `HyperlinkedModelSerializer` / `rest_framework.serializers.*` → honorary DRF serializer.\n   - wagtail activation: `Page` / `wagtail.models.Page` / `wagtail.Page` → honorary Wagtail Page.\n5. Maintenance: single-module home (e.g. `linkers/_third_party_bases.py`) with a property test asserting (a) no duplicate simple names within a framework activation set, (b) every entry has at least one FQN-prefixed alias. Stale-entry detection lives in the bakeoff feedback loop, not in manual audits.\n\n## Validation\n\nAfter implementation, re-run the bakeoff cycle against pretix + a Wagtail target + a DRF target and confirm rescue counts approximately reproduce the rates measured here. Tag the implementation PR with `awaits_bakeoff_validation` per the validation-tagging discipline.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- AC-1: A Python class whose only base is an external `HierarkeyForm` receives a `django_orm` `dispatches_to` edge for its `save` / `clean` / `delete` overrides, with the same shape (`evidence_type=naming_convention` or equivalent) used by direct-Model rescues today.\n- AC-2: Same for FilterSet, DRF Serializer family, Wagtail Page, ModelAdmin — each gated on its respective framework activation.\n- AC-3: A non-Django repo (e.g., one of the 15 from the report's FP corpus) emits zero edges from the new allow-list logic. Property test asserts the framework-activation gate works as a hard cutoff.\n- AC-4: 100% coverage on the new module. Defensive paths marked `# pragma: no cover` with rationale.\n\n## References\n\n- Data pass report: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wi-jusih-data-pass-20260515/report.md`\n- Parent: WI-jusih-navod-mogib-disot-busub-rapof-susol-baniv\n- WI-jusih UAT origin: round-03 master report DQ-1 (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-03-WI-nosug-django-transitive-and-dispatch-revalidation/report.md`)\n- INV-zuhub: short-name fallback discipline (`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/_transitive_bases.py::build_short_name_collisions`, `short_name_fallback`)\n- Existing BFS: `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/_transitive_bases.py::collect_transitive_base_names`\n- Existing simple-name fallback: `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/inheritance.py:175-194`"  # 2916
